   "text": "The drawing shows a lutetium(III) texaphyrin complex (motexafin lutetium type). It has five components: the macrocycle, Lu\u00b3\u207a, one water, and two acetate anions.\n\n**Macrocycle, read region by region:**\n- **Top pyrrole:** a 3-hydroxypropyl group and a methyl group on the \u03b2-carbons. Its nitrogen is a plain imine-type N.\n- **Left pyrrole:** two ethyl groups on the \u03b2-carbons. Its nitrogen carries the negative charge, [N-].\n- **Bottom pyrrole:** a methyl group and a 3-hydroxypropyl group on the \u03b2-carbons. Its nitrogen is also a plain imine-type N.\n- **Benzene unit:** it is joined to the rest of the macrocycle through two C=N bonds. Each of its two remaining ring carbons carries an O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH3 chain (triethylene glycol monomethyl ether).\n- **Bridges:** CH= links join the pyrroles to each other and to the imine nitrogens.\n\nThe drawing shows no wedges, hashes or cis/trans geometry, so the SMILES has no stereo marks.\n\n**Kekul\u00e9 form I used:**\n- The two benzene double bonds that remain in the ring are the one next to each ether carbon.\n- The two benzene carbons attached to the imine nitrogens carry exocyclic C=N bonds instead.\n\nI assembled the SMILES by hand and traced it atom by atom against the drawing, but did not run it through a parser.\n\nSMILES: C1(CCCO)=C(C)C2=CN=C3C=C(OCCOCCOCCOC)C(OCCOCCOCCOC)=CC3=NC=C4C(C)=C(CCCO)C(=N4)C=C5C(CC)=C(CC)C(=CC1=N2)[N-]5.[Lu+3].O.CC(=O)[O-].CC(=O)[O-]"
